---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Read messages from a topic and print them as they arrive

Usage: rustman kafka consume [OPTIONS] [REQUEST]

Arguments:
  [REQUEST]
          A request file, its id or its name; without one, the flags describe the operation

Options:
      --brokers <HOST:PORT>
          Bootstrap brokers: host:port, comma-separated

      --topic <NAME>
          The topic

      --partition <N>
          Read this partition (repeatable; default: all)

      --offset <OFFSET>
          Where to start: earliest, latest (default), an offset, or an RFC 3339 timestamp

      --max-messages <N>
          Stop after N messages (default: the request's limits.max_messages, else 10)

      --duration <DURATION>
          Stop after this long (default: the request's limits.duration_ms, else 30s)

      --json
          Print one JSON object per message

      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --var <K=V>
          Set a variable, above every other source (repeatable): --var k=v

      --no-history
          Do not record the operation in history

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
